==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
This stage can potentially be cleared before the Project A spawns and without giving Metal One Horn a chance to push if you bring [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]] and [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]] as meatshields, [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]] to kill the Metal enemies, and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] to rush the base. If Hurricat's crits aren't in your favor and the major threats do spawn, you can reset, but Rover's warp blocking and Bahamut's sheer damage output should be able to take out Project A regardless, or the meatshields might slip past and finish off the already-damaged base.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
With the addition of UltraBaaBaa to this stage in chapter 2 you will need a barrier breaker in addition to a source of critical hits and ways to handle the aliens when compared to chapter 1. If you have [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Marine Cat]] they can handle both the metal enemies and the UltraBaaBaa's barriers, leaving your other 4 units to be dedicated to meatshields and ways to handle the aliens. Do note that this would likely be less feasible without the true form for Space Cat due to their lower proc chance, but they may still be usable. Alternatively, a unit like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] can be used to handle the metals, while a different barrier breaker is used for UltraBaaBaa, if you have Catasaurus but not Space Marine. Simply make use of what good critter and barrier breakers you have, and use your remaining slots to handle the rest as you would most alien stages, just with a low slot count, so pick your anti-alien choices wisely. If you have a unit from the [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|Elemental Pixies]] banner, they would likely do very well here, especially as they can also break UltraBaaBaa's barriers, helping to kill the second and third ones more easily if needed.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Due to this restriction, you should bring only units that are necessary. These units include barrier breakers like [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kitty of Liberty]] and Critical Hitters such as [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]]. You should also bring a heavy damage dealer like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to deal with the Star Pengs and Ribbos. In addition, you can bring other units like crowd-controllers or nukers to assist your units by stopping enemies from killing your Critical Hitters.

==='''Rush Strategy (Chapter 3)'''===
Loadout: [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Miss Moneko]], [[Crazed Moneko (Special Cat)|Crazed Moneko]], [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|The Kitty Of Liberty]], [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat/Catornado]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]].

For this strategy, you need to have good luck. First, spawn a Miss Moneko to kill some peons, and when you have the money spawn Catornado and Kitty Of Liberty right away. If both of them end up dying at any point, close the app and start over. Once the UltraBaaBaa and Metal Doge die, spawn any other critters you might have to kill the Metal Hippoes in advance. They should give you enough money to summon Awakened Bahamut, meanwhile all the other Cats advance and kill the remaining support before Project A. has a chance to spawn.

